From 5200aaa49936ad3c88ea0af145cac434c9be236b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 03:17:30 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 03/59] ntdll: Run on arm64 macOS without low 4G remapping and
 with 16K pages.

- Relocate the shared user data page above PAGEZERO when 0x7ffe0000 can't be
  mapped, publish its address to PE ntdll (__wine_user_shared_data) and unix
  modules (ntdll_get_user_shared_data), and emulate ARM64 loads that fault on
  the canonical address in the SIGSEGV handler.
- Emulate W+X host pages, which the kernel refuses without MAP_JIT, by
  flipping them between RX and RW on write and execute faults.
